---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy" description="How the tools I build use your information: as little as possible." path="/privacy">
  <article class="policy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">I build small tools so people can make things together, like shared slide decks at decks.gszep.com. I don't sell, share or analyse your data. There are no ads and no trackers.</p>

    <h2>When you sign in with Google</h2>
    <p>Google tells me your email address and an account ID. That's all I ask for. I use it to check that something has been shared with you, and to show collaborators who you are. I never see your password, contacts, files or anything else in your Google account.</p>

    <h2>What gets kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your email address and name, on the sharing list of the things shared with you.</li>
      <li>What you create or edit, with your name and the time, so collaborators can see who changed what, plus a short edit history for undo.</li>
      <li>Standard server logs kept by Google Cloud for a limited time, for security and fixing problems.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you connect an AI agent, its sign-in stays on your own computer. Your agent can only do what you can do, and never overwrites text a person has edited.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>Only the ones needed to keep you signed in or to remember a password you entered. No analytics or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>Where it lives and who sees it</h2>
    <p>On Google Cloud and GitHub. Only I and the people something is shared with can see it.</p>

    <h2>Removing yourself</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@gszep.com">contact@gszep.com</a> and I'll remove your details, and your name from your edits if you like.</p>

    <p class="updated">If anything here changes, I'll update this page. Last updated 30 September 2026. See also the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  .policy { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .policy h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .policy .lede { font-size: 1.125rem; }
  .policy p, .policy li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .policy ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .policy a { text-decoration: underline; }
  .policy .updated { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem; opacity: 0.7; }
</style>
